      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "When the studies used the same sample as another study, the more representative (precise) one was maintained in the analysis as the dataset, and the other(s) were used if they presented different variables from the first study.",
      "reason": "The evidence describes grouping/selection rules affecting syntheses (e.g., choosing more representative samples/datasets), but it does not clearly specify the groups used in each synthesis and link them to comparisons defined in the review objectives."
